  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656522",
      "title": "Reactive: Creating a Custom Async Validator",
      "lectureOrder": 538,
      "videoOrder": 493,
      "sourceHash": "8a8030b9e5027c7c580d935ed352c383df2b75c169705dd4e3d245bc66c7b938",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 3.233,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.233,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "we saw how we can use these error codes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 9.93,
          "en": "and we also saw that we can add our own validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.93,
          "end": 13.35,
          "en": "We checked if the name is invalid, the username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.35,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "but typically you might need to reach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 18.54,
          "en": "out to a web server to check this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "That, however, is a asynchronous operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 24.72,
          "en": "because the response is not coming back instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.72,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "Instead, it just takes a couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "So we also kind of need asynchronous validators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 36.51,
          "en": "which are able to wait for a response before, well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "returning, True or false, is it valid or not?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "Turns out we can create such asynchronous validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "So let's create one here in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 48.837,
          "en": "I'll name it, \"forbiddenEmails.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.01,
          "end": 53.76,
          "en": "This asynchronous validator also takes the control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.76,
          "end": 55.203,
          "en": "as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "Now we also need to return something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "but this will not be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "with an error code and a bullion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "Instead, this will a be a promise which wraps anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "or an observable which wraps anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "For the observable, you need to import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 75.06,
          "en": "from rxjs/Observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "And, these are of course two constructs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "which handle asynchronous data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "That's exactly what this validator is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.42,
          "end": 88.68,
          "en": "So here, I now want to create a promise in this validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.68,
          "end": 90.28,
          "en": "A new promise it will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "which returns us anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "And as all promises, this receives a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 99.99000000000001,
          "en": "with resolve and rechecked as arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "we can execute in that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "and in that function, I now want to set a timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "After one and a half seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "I want to return a response to simulate the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "that we have a asynchronous task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 114.96000000000001,
          "en": "like reaching out to a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.96000000000001,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "So this will be the function which gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "after one and a half seconds, this anonymous function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "And here, I will simply check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 127.67,
          "en": "if control value equals test@test.com.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "Of course, we could also check if it's part of an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "I will simply check for this single email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "If this is the case, validation failed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "and as in the synchronous validator case this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "when I will return an object with a key value pair",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "with this error code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 148.98,
          "en": "Here, of course, since we are in a promise I don't return,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.98,
          "end": 153.66,
          "en": "I resolve, and again, I resolve this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.66,
          "end": 158.66,
          "en": "where I say, \"emailIsForbidden,\" like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 160.623,
          "en": "set this to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.61,
          "end": 165.54,
          "en": "and if we pass this check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.54,
          "end": 169.14,
          "en": "so in the else case, that we have a valid input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.14,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "that we have a valid email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.48,
          "en": "I will simply resolve null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 178.113,
          "en": "Now of course, we need to return this promise in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 182.82,
          "en": "So with this we set up our asynchronous validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "Now we can add it. Let's add it to the email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 186.75,
          "en": "And here you don't add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.75,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "in this array of normal validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "Instead we use deferred argument we can pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "to form control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 197.13,
          "en": "This is asynchronous validator or an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.13,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "of such validators, just like the normal validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "but reserve for the asynchronous ones.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 207.5,
          "en": "So here I will use my forbidden emails validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 212.55,
          "en": "Again, don't execute it, simply pass the reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 214.92000000000002,
          "en": "And you need to bind this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.92000000000002,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "If you plan on using this in there, I don't,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 219.81,
          "en": "so I don't need to do it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "Now let's check if it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 226.52,
          "en": "If we compile this and we inspect the email, it's invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "If I enter something here, you see it stays invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 233.94299999999998,
          "en": "If I enter test two, closely, watch ng-invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 237.84,
          "en": "Did you see that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 240.3,
          "en": "It changed to ng-pending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.3,
          "end": 243.03,
          "en": "because it was evaluating the input?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.03,
          "end": 245.58,
          "en": "Then it changed to ng-valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.58,
          "end": 247.47,
          "en": "Now if I remove the two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.47,
          "end": 249.96,
          "en": "and therefore I will enter an invalid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.96,
          "end": 252.48,
          "en": "because that's the one we're checking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.48,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "It again, switches to pending and then to invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 259.32,
          "en": "So this is now how the asynchronous validator works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.32,
          "end": 261.75,
          "en": "and of course, this would work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 265.47,
          "en": "with code where you reach out to the web, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.47,
          "end": 267.09,
          "en": "and we correctly therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.09,
          "end": 269.31,
          "en": "see our error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.31,
          "end": 272.34000000000003,
          "en": "So, these are asynchronous validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.34000000000003,
          "end": 275.01,
          "en": "Really easy to add when using the reactive approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.01,
          "end": 275.883,
          "en": "as you saw.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
